{% endcomment %}## Status map

- `Backlog` -> out of scope for this workflow; do not modify, except when an escape hatch returns the issue to `Backlog` for human input or external unblock.
- `Todo` -> queued; immediately transition to `In Progress` before active work.
  - Special case: if a PR is already attached, treat as feedback/rework loop (run full PR feedback sweep, address or explicitly push back, revalidate, return to `In Review`).
- `In Progress` -> implementation actively underway.
- `Waiting on sub-tickets` -> a `breakdown` parent whose plan a human approved, waiting on its sub-tickets; do nothing. Symphony promotes its `Backlog` sub-tickets to `Todo` on entry, and starts the parent's close-out run from here once every sub-ticket is terminal (see `Parent tickets`). Any other ticket lands here when its PR merges with sub-tickets still open: Symphony promotes its `Backlog` sub-tickets to `Todo` and moves it to `Done` itself, with no run, once every sub-ticket is terminal; do nothing. One a person moved here without its PR merging waits for them.
- `Auto Review` -> Symphony is testing the PR as a user and, with the acceptance gate on, judging it against the ticket's acceptance criteria; do not change the issue or PR, wait.
- `In Review` -> PR is attached and validated (or, for a `breakdown` parent, its plan is in the workpad); waiting on human approval. With the acceptance gate in `enforce` mode it holds only the gate's escalations, since the gate moves its approves to `Merging` and its reworks to `In Progress` itself; with the gate off or in `shadow`, every PR waits here. A person's comment on a `breakdown` plan under review brings the parent back to `In Progress` for a plan revision run (see `Parent tickets`).
- `Human Review` -> waiting on the operator only, apart from the supervisor's `In Review` queue: an Auto Review QA block only a person can clear, a plan whose ticket says a human reviews it, an open `linear_request_human_action` request, or a final verification whose remaining checks are manual. Symphony never dispatches it; do not change the issue or PR, wait. A person's move out of it counts like one out of `In Review` (to `Merging`, `Rework`, `Waiting on sub-tickets` or `Done`). A supervisor moves a ticket here when it needs the operator, and never approves out of it on their behalf.
- `Merging` -> approved by a human, or by the acceptance gate in `enforce` mode; follow the repo's landing flow to merge (do not call `gh pr merge` directly). With the gate in `enforce` mode, a push that changes the PR's own diff (not a merge of the base branch) sends it back to `Auto Review`, where the gate judges the new head.
- `Rework` -> reviewer requested changes; planning + implementation required.
- `Done` -> terminal state; no further action required.
